In this modified version of the code, we first read the input from the user using the `Scanner.nextLine()` method. We then wrap the code that attempts to parse the input as an integer in a `try` block. If the input is not a valid integer, the `NumberFormatException` will be caught, and an error message will be displayed.

This approach ensures that your program does not crash due to an `InputMismatchException`, and provides a more user-friendly experience for the user.

