Here's an example Google Apps Script that searches for a place name in a column and stores the latitude and longitude in other columns:

```javascript
function searchPlace() {
  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getActiveSheet();
  var dataRange = sheet.getRange("A2:B"); // Assuming your data is in columns A and B, starting from row 2
  var values = dataRange.getValues();

  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    var placeName = values[i][0];
    var url = "https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?address=" + placeName + "&key=YOUR_API_KEY";

    var response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(url);
    var json = JSON.parse(response);

    if (json.results.length > 0) {
      var latitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lat;
      var longitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lng;

      sheet.getRange(i + 2, 3).setValue(latitude);
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, 4).setValue(longitude);
    } else {
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, 3).setValue("");
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, 4).setValue("");
    }
  }
}
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key. This script will search for the place name in column A, starting from row 2, and store the latitude and longitude in columns C and D, respectively.

Here's the PHP custom function "smart_sort_array" as requested:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function ($a, $b) use ($order) {
        if ($a['age'] == $b['age']) {
            return 0;
        }
        return $order === 'asc' ? $a['age'] - $b['age'] : $b['age'] - $a['age'];
    });
    return $set;
}
```

