To pass credentials in your JS code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the required dependencies:

```bash
npm install react-native-fbsdk-next
```

2. Create a new file called `Credentials.js` and add the following code:

```javascript
import { Facebook } from 'react-native-fbsdk-next';

const Credentials = {
  appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID', // Replace with your Facebook App ID
  apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY', // Replace with your Facebook API Key
};

export default Credentials;
```

3. In your main application file (e.g., `App.js`), import the `Credentials` object and use it when initializing the Facebook SDK:

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { Facebook } from 'react-native-fbsdk-next';
import Credentials from './Credentials';

const App = () => {
  const [isLoggedIn, setIsLoggedIn] = useState(false);

  const handleLogin = async () => {
    try {
      await Facebook.loginWithReadPermissionsAsync(Credentials.appId);
      setIsLoggedIn(true);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error logging in:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      <Button title="Login with Facebook" onPress={handleLogin} />
      {isLoggedIn && <Text>Logged in successfully!</Text>}
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;
```

Replace `YOUR_APP_ID` and `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Facebook App ID and API Key.

Now, when you run your application, it will use the provided credentials to initialize the Facebook SDK and allow users to log in with their Facebook accounts.

